  "activity": {
    "id": "act_retrograde_motion",
    "name": "Solving the Puzzle of Retrograde Motion",
    "description": "A hands-on AR investigation of apparent retrograde motion. Learners first watch Mars trace its westward loop across the constellations from Earth's surface, then step outside the solar system to see how the loop emerges naturally from Earth overtaking Mars on its faster inner orbit. Students compare geocentric epicycles to the heliocentric explanation, predict when retrograde occurs, and contrast the loops of Mars, Jupiter, and Saturn.",
    "language": "en",
    "workplace": "wp_retrograde_motion",
    "start": "action_intro",
    "actions": [
      {
        "id": "action_intro",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "dev_hololens",
        "location": "place_earth_station",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "Welcome: The Wandering Planets",
          "description": "The ancient Greeks called the planets 'wanderers' because they drift against the fixed stars. But sometimes a planet like Mars seems to stop, reverse, and loop backward. This lab will let you solve that puzzle. When you are ready, say or click 'Begin' to observe Mars from Earth's surface."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "person_learner",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_intro_audio"
            },
            {
              "target": "place_earth_station",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_starfield_backdrop",
              "poi": "default",
              "viewport": "actions"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": true,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "person_learner",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_intro_audio"
            },
            {
              "target": "place_earth_station",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_starfield_backdrop"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "action_observe_sky",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          },
          {
            "mode": "voice",
            "id": "action_observe_sky",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "action_observe_sky",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "dev_hololens",
        "location": "place_sky_dome",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "Step 1: Watch Mars Loop in the Night Sky",
          "description": "Look up at the night-sky dome. Mars is marked in red against the constellations. Watch the time-lapse: over several weeks Mars drifts slowly EASTWARD, then slows, reverses into a WESTWARD loop for about two months, then resumes eastward. This backward loop is 'apparent retrograde motion'. When you have traced the full loop, click 'Next'."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "place_sky_dome",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_starfield_backdrop",
              "poi": "poi_zenith"
            },
            {
              "target": "place_sky_dome",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_mars_loop_anim",
              "poi": "poi_zenith",
              "state": "eastward_then_loop"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_mars_globe",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_label_mars",
              "poi": "poi_mars_label",
              "text": "Mars: watch it reverse!"
            },
            {
              "target": "person_learner",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_mars_narration"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": true,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "place_sky_dome",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "*"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_mars_globe",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_label_mars"
            },
            {
              "target": "person_learner",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_mars_narration"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "action_geocentric",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          },
          {
            "mode": "voice",
            "id": "action_geocentric",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "action_geocentric",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "dev_hololens",
        "location": "place_orrery",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "Step 2: The Old Geocentric Fix \u2014 Epicycles",
          "description": "How did ancient astronomers explain the loop with Earth at the center? They added an 'epicycle' \u2014 a small circle riding on Mars's larger orbit \u2014 so Mars could momentarily move backward. Notice how complicated this is. Click 'Next' to test a simpler idea."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "place_orrery",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_geocentric_epicycle",
              "poi": "poi_sun_center",
              "state": "earth_centered"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_earth_globe",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_label_earth",
              "poi": "poi_earth_label",
              "text": "Earth (assumed center)"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_mars_globe",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_label_mars",
              "poi": "poi_mars_label",
              "text": "Mars on an awkward epicycle"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": true,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "place_orrery",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_geocentric_epicycle"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_earth_globe",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_label_earth"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_mars_globe",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_label_mars"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "action_heliocentric",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          },
          {
            "mode": "voice",
            "id": "action_heliocentric",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "action_heliocentric",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "dev_hololens",
        "location": "place_space_station",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "Step 3: Step Outside \u2014 The Heliocentric View",
          "description": "Now fly outside the solar system to the orrery table. The Sun is at the center; Earth and Mars move in smooth circles \u2014 no epicycles needed. Watch Earth, on its faster inner orbit, catch up to and OVERTAKE the slower Mars. The green sightlines show what you'd see from Earth: as we pass Mars, it appears to drift backward \u2014 just like a car you overtake on the highway. Click 'Next'."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "place_orrery",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_heliocentric_orbits",
              "poi": "poi_sun_center",
              "state": "orbits_running"
            },
            {
              "target": "place_orrery",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_overtaking_arrows",
              "poi": "poi_earth_orbit"
            },
            {
              "target": "place_orrery",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_sightline_diagram",
              "poi": "poi_mars_orbit"
            },
            {
              "target": "place_orrery",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_label_sun",
              "poi": "poi_sun_center",
              "text": "Sun (true center)"
            },
            {
              "target": "person_learner",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_helio_narration"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": true,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "place_orrery",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "*"
            },
            {
              "target": "person_learner",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_helio_narration"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [],
